.TP
.B bus
.RI (string,\ default:\ "i2c")
Transport:
.B i2c
or
.BR spi .
SPI is faster per transfer, which is what unlocks the high sample rates and
shortens the FIFO drain.
Not every driver has SPI; the daemon refuses to start on one that does not.
The IMU and the magnetometer choose independently, so a SPI IMU alongside an
I2C compass is a legal rig.
.TP
.B spi_dev
.RI (string,\ default:\ "")
spidev node, for example
.IR /dev/spidev0.0 .
Required when
.BR "bus = \(dqspi\(dq" ;
ignored otherwise.
The chip select in the node name does the addressing, so
.B i2c_addr
is unused.
.TP
.B spi_speed_hz
.RI (int,\ default:\ 0)
SPI clock in Hz.
.B 0
means the driver's datasheet maximum, which is the useful default.
A request above that maximum is clamped rather than refused, and the daemon
logs the rate it really programmed.
.TP
.B i2c_addr
.RI (int,\ default:\ 0x6B)
I2C address; used only when
.BR "bus = \(dqi2c\(dq" .
ISM330DHCX: 0x6B (SA0 high) or 0x6A (SA0 low).
.TP
.B int_gpio
.RI (int,\ default:\ 17)
BCM GPIO number for the FIFO watermark interrupt.
Set
.B 0
to use a 10\~ms polling timer instead.
.TP
.B odr_hz
.RI (int,\ default:\ 833)
Output data rate in Hz; must be greater than zero.
A rate the chip cannot produce is rounded
.I up
to the next one it can, and the filter is tuned for that actual rate; the
daemon logs both at startup when they differ.
ISM330DHCX supports: 12, 26, 52, 104, 208, 416, 833, 1660, 3332, 6664.
Rates above 1660 need
.BR "bus = \(dqspi\(dq" .
.TP
.B accel_g
.RI (int,\ default:\ 8)
Accelerometer full-scale range in g.
ISM330DHCX: 2, 4, 8, 16.
.TP
.B gyro_dps
.RI (int,\ default:\ 2000)
Gyroscope full-scale range in degrees/second.
ISM330DHCX: 125, 250, 500, 1000, 2000, 4000.
.TP
.B fifo_wm
.RI (int,\ default:\ 64)
FIFO watermark in sample-sets.
At 833\~Hz, 32 ~= 38\~ms latency; 64 ~= 77\~ms.
