.SS [position]
Magnetic declination and true heading.
.B [hot]:
declination_deg, lat_deg, lon_deg, wmm_file (declination and the WMM field
reference are recomputed on SIGHUP; a live position source \(em gpsd or
SignalK \(em owns declination while enabled).
.B [restart]:
the gpsd_* and signalk_* source keys and fix_max_age_h.
.PP
When declination is active, imud emits
.B $HCHDT
in NMEA and sets
.B FLAG_DECLINATION_VALID
(with the
.B declination_deg
field) in the binary packet.
.PP
Three modes (highest priority wins):
.TP
1.\ WMM\ auto-compute
Set
.B lat_deg
and
.B lon_deg
(both non-zero).
imud loads
.B wmm_file
and computes declination at startup and on SIGHUP.
Accurate to \(+-0.5\(de for a fixed installation.
.TP
2.\ Static\ override
Set
.B declination_deg
only (leave lat/lon at 0.0).
East declination is positive (+), west is negative (\-).
.TP
3.\ Disabled\ (default)
All three values at zero.
.PP
Configuration keys:
.\" BEGIN GENERATED: config-keys position
.TP
.B declination_deg
.RI (float,\ default:\ 0.0)
Static magnetic declination in degrees.
Ignored when
.B lat_deg
and
.B lon_deg
are both non-zero.
.TP
.B lat_deg
.RI (double,\ default:\ 0.0)
Geodetic latitude in decimal degrees (+N / \-S).
Set with
.B lon_deg
to enable WMM auto-compute.
.TP
.B lon_deg
.RI (double,\ default:\ 0.0)
Geodetic longitude in decimal degrees (+E / \-W).
.TP
.B wmm_file
.RI (string,\ default:\ \(dq\(dq\ =\ auto)
Path to the WMM coefficient file.
When empty (the default), imud uses
.I /etc/imud/WMM.COF
if it exists (operator override), otherwise
.I /usr/share/imud/WMM.COF
(installed by the imud-wmm-data package /
.BR "make install-wmm-data" ).
The bundled model is WMM2025, valid 2025.0\(en2030.0.
When WMM2030 is published (expected late 2029), update the data package \(em
or drop the new file in as an override:
.EX
    sudo cp WMM2030.COF /etc/imud/WMM.COF
    sudo systemctl reload imud
.EE
.TP
.B gpsd_enabled
.RI (bool,\ default:\ false)
Connect to gpsd for live position updates.
.TP
.B gpsd_host
.RI (string,\ default:\ \(dqlocalhost\(dq)
Hostname or IP address of the gpsd instance.
.TP
.B gpsd_port
.RI (int,\ default:\ 2947)
TCP port of the gpsd instance.
.TP
.B signalk_enabled
.RI (bool,\ default:\ false)
Poll the SignalK REST API for position (every 30\~s).
.TP
.B signalk_host
.RI (string,\ default:\ \(dqlocalhost\(dq)
Hostname or IP address of the SignalK server.
.TP
.B signalk_port
.RI (int,\ default:\ 3000)
HTTP port of the SignalK server.
.TP
.B signalk_path
.RI (string,\ default:\ \(dq/signalk/v1/api/vessels/self/navigation/position\(dq)
REST endpoint path.
.TP
.B fix_max_age_h
.RI (float,\ default:\ 24.0)
Hours to retain a GPS-derived declination without a new fix.
An anchored vessel with continuous GPS reception keeps its declination
indefinitely; the TTL only fires during a genuine GPS outage.
Set
.B 0
to never expire.
